From c2422084ac31c6767e6adc875bbcda1405dce2fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:02:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] RDNA4 dense row concat across a K-quant / Q6_K pair
 (attn_v of the K-quant M mixes)

The RDNA4 1-token dense row concat runs the Q / K / V projections over the same input in one ksplit launch, but only
when all three weights share a type.  In the K-quant M files attn_v is Q6_K in about half the layers (Q / K Q4_K, Q5_K
or IQ4_XS), so V runs alone there.  The ksplit kernel becomes a device body; mul_mat_vec_q_ksplit_cat2 runs the Q6_K
body for the row blocks of that segment (with its own row stride) and the launch type's body for the rest.  Both types
take the same nwarps on RDNA4 and each row keeps its own one-warp dot product, so every row computes what its
standalone launch does.  The type is chosen once per block, so the decode grid loop is off for these launches; the
matcher takes either graph order (V comes first) and requires the launch tensor to be the largest.
GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_ROW_CONCAT_MIXED=0: off.

Qwen3-30B-A3B Q4_K_M, 1x R9700: tg128 169.74 -> 171.73 (+1.2 %, 6 + 6 runs ABBA, -r 20), 518 -> 494 launches/token;
server replies identical on/off (Qwen3-30B, Qwen3.6-35B, Llama-3.2-1B); decode-path KLD (-b 1 -ub 1) 0.
Qwen3.6-35B-A3B: 6 mixed layers per token, -6 launches.
